line 37 True, line 38: '' in _ws? `'' in \" \\t\\n\\r\"` \u2192 True! Empty string is \"in\" any string. Hmm, `'' in _ws` is True because empty string is a substring. So line 39: end = _w(s, 1).end() \u2192 WHITESPACE.match(s, 1) with len(s)=1 \u2192 matches empty at 1, end=1. nextchar = s[1:2] = ''. Line 42: '' != '}'. Line 44: '' != '\"' \u2192 raise JSONDecodeError at pos 1. OK, that also works. But `{,}` is cleaner.\n\n**Case E: missing colon** \u2014 `{\"a\" 1}`: \n- 0='{',1='\"',2='a',3='\"',4=' ',5='1',6='}'.\n- end=1 \u2192 nextchar='\"' \u2192 end=2. scanstring(s,2) \u2192 ('a',4). s[4:5]=' ' != ':' \u2192 end=_w(s,4).end()=5. s[5:6]='1' != ':' \u2192 raise JSONDecodeError(\"Expecting ':' delimiter\", s, 5).\n\nCovers line 58 True \u2192 line 59.\n\n**Case F: truncated after colon (IndexError at line 63)** \u2014 `{\"a\":`:\n- 0='{',1='\"',2='a',3='\"',4=':'. end=1 \u2192 nextchar='\"' \u2192 end=2. scanstring \u2192 ('a',4). s[4:5]=':' \u2192 end=5. Line 63: s[5] \u2192 IndexError \u2192 line 67-68 pass. scan_once(s, 5): fake raises StopIteration(5) \u2192 line 72-73: raise JSONDecodeError(\"Expecting value\", s, 5).\n\nCovers 67-68, 72-73.\n\nHmm wait, but with a fake scan_once that raises StopIteration only when told... Let me make the fake scan_once behave like the real one: raise StopIteration(idx) if it can't parse at idx. For `{\"a\":` at idx=5 (past end), raise StopIteration(5). Actually the real C scanner raises StopIteration with the value being the position... In CPython's C scanner, `scan_once` raises StopIteration(err.value) where err.value is set. For the Python scanner (`py_make_scanner`), on IndexError it raises StopIteration(idx)? Let me recall json/scanner.py:\n\n```python\ndef py_make_scanner(context):\n    parse_object = JSONObject\n    ...\n    def scanner(string, idx):\n        try:\n            nextchar = string[idx]\n        except IndexError:\n            raise StopIteration(idx) from None\n        ...\n    return scanner\n```\n\nYe